   <description>
      <p>theatr.us PixInsight repository: scripts and tools for narrowband palette work.</p>
      <p>Add https://pixinsight.theatr.us/ under Resources &gt; Updates &gt; Manage Repositories. The older address https://pixinsight.psf-guard.com/ keeps working.</p>
   </description>
   <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.9.4:1.9.99">
      <package fileName="FPU_202610202042.zip" sha1="2e44792da40f3270cdd6205277792dfef9a03462" type="script" releaseDate="20261020" serverURL="https://pixinsight.theatr.us/">
         <title>Foraxx Palette Utility 2.5.0</title>
         <description>
            <p>Builds a Foraxx (or SHO, HOO, HSO, OHS) palette image from stretched, starless narrowband images, plus an optional stars image. The Foraxx palette is The Coldest Nights&apos; dynamic narrowband combination (https://thecoldestnights.com/). Adds a zoomable preview, mask bias and contrast, per-channel midtones, channel-ratio masks, protected saturation and a colour-preserving L* curve. Rewritten for the V8 JavaScript runtime in PixInsight 1.9.4. Installs under Script &gt; theatr.us.</p>
            <p>Original script by Paul Hancock, Paulyman Astro. Copyright (c) 2023-2024 Paul Hancock. Copyright (c) 2026 Yann Ramin, Apache License 2.0. Source: https://github.com/theatrus/foraxx-palette-utility</p>
         </description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
